# finale(Player player)
#
# The last beat of the cutscene, fired once the ring has finished
# dissolving into the child. Two parts:
#
#   THE BANG    a flash, an explosion emitter and layered sound on the
#               stand's chest, all on one tick.
#   THE WHEEL   finaleArms rainbow spiral arms sweeping outward across
#               the ground around the stand at finaleY, drawn one ring of
#               particles per tick for finaleTicks.
#
# The wheel runs in two phases. Out to finaleSplitRadius it is one wave,
# expanding on an ease-OUT curve — most of the distance covered in the
# first half-second, then slowing as it widens. That is the shape a blast
# wave actually has, and it puts the energy on the bang rather than
# dribbling outward at a constant rate. On finaleSplitTick it arrives,
# and hands off.
#
# Phase two puts finaleCentres equidistant points ON that ring, each the
# centre of its own mini spiral. The streams do two things at once: they
# slide along the ring into the centre that feeds them, and they begin
# orbiting it. Both start at zero on the split tick, so every stream is
# still exactly where phase one left it — the big wheel weaves into the
# small ones with nothing jumping. The orbits then bloom and wind back
# in, so the whole thing drains into finaleCentres points and vanishes.
#
# Consecutive streams share a centre (a / perCentre, not a % centres), so
# a contiguous run of the ring folds into one whirl instead of every
# third stream crossing the others to get there.
#
# ROOM: 7 blocks across, stand at the centre, so nothing may pass 3.5
# blocks out. The whirl centres ride the 2.5 ring and their orbits bloom
# 0.9 past it, for a hard maximum of 3.4. Since an orbit swings its
# stream radially outward as well as in, that sum — not the ring alone —
# is what has to clear finaleMaxRadius.
#
# COLOUR: rainbowColors is a full hue wheel, evenly spaced in OKLCH (an
# RGB rainbow bunches up in the cyans and races through the oranges) with
# each band drawn at its own gamut cusp — the lightness where that
# particular hue holds the most chroma. Blue peaks near L 0.45 and yellow
# up at 0.87, so a wheel drawn at a single lightness is vivid at two
# hues and chalky everywhere else.
#
# The wheel is indexed with pure Int maths — tick and arm, never an angle
# — so no Double-to-Int conversion is needed anywhere. Each arm sits
# rainbowArmOffset bands round the wheel from the last, and the whole
# thing advances rainbowStep bands a tick, so the arms are different
# colours at any instant AND each arm cycles as it sweeps.
#
# DO NOT hand-edit the table below — it is generated by
# irodori_gradient.py at the repo root alongside the other colour tables.
@using irodoriAnimation
@fast

@define String[] rainbowColors = String["1.000,0.000,0.533", "1.000,0.000,0.495", "1.000,0.000,0.458", "1.000,0.000,0.419", "1.000,0.000,0.380", "1.000,0.000,0.340", "1.000,0.000,0.296", "1.000,0.000,0.248", "1.000,0.000,0.192", "1.000,0.000,0.115", "1.000,0.083,0.000", "1.000,0.211,0.000", "1.000,0.283,0.000", "1.000,0.337,0.000", "1.000,0.381,0.000", "1.000,0.418,0.000", "1.000,0.452,0.000", "1.000,0.483,0.000", "1.000,0.511,0.000", "1.000,0.538,0.000", "1.000,0.563,0.000", "1.000,0.588,0.000", "1.000,0.611,0.000", "1.000,0.634,0.000", "1.000,0.657,0.000", "1.000,0.680,0.000", "1.000,0.702,0.000", "1.000,0.725,0.000", "1.000,0.748,0.000", "1.000,0.772,0.000", "1.000,0.797,0.000", "1.000,0.822,0.000", "1.000,0.849,0.000", "1.000,0.878,0.000", "1.000,0.908,0.000", "1.000,0.941,0.000", "1.000,0.977,0.000", "0.983,1.000,0.000", "0.942,1.000,0.000", "0.898,1.000,0.000", "0.852,1.000,0.000", "0.802,1.000,0.000", "0.747,1.000,0.000", "0.686,1.000,0.000", "0.615,1.000,0.000", "0.531,1.000,0.000", "0.422,1.000,0.000", "0.249,1.000,0.000", "0.000,1.000,0.223", "0.000,1.000,0.377", "0.000,1.000,0.472", "0.000,1.000,0.543", "0.000,1.000,0.601", "0.000,1.000,0.650", "0.000,1.000,0.693", "0.000,1.000,0.731", "0.000,1.000,0.765", "0.000,1.000,0.797", "0.000,1.000,0.827", "0.000,1.000,0.855", "0.000,1.000,0.881", "0.000,1.000,0.907", "0.000,1.000,0.931", "0.000,1.000,0.955", "0.000,1.000,0.979", "0.000,0.998,1.000", "0.000,0.976,1.000", "0.000,0.954,1.000", "0.000,0.933,1.000", "0.000,0.913,1.000", "0.000,0.893,1.000", "0.000,0.874,1.000", "0.000,0.854,1.000", "0.000,0.835,1.000", "0.000,0.815,1.000", "0.000,0.795,1.000", "0.000,0.775,1.000", "0.000,0.754,1.000", "0.000,0.732,1.000", "0.000,0.709,1.000", "0.000,0.684,1.000", "0.000,0.658,1.000", "0.000,0.630,1.000", "0.000,0.598,1.000", "0.000,0.562,1.000", "0.000,0.520,1.000", "0.000,0.467,1.000", "0.000,0.395,1.000", "0.124,0.362,1.000", "0.199,0.349,1.000", "0.252,0.336,1.000", "0.296,0.322,1.000", "0.334,0.306,1.000", "0.368,0.289,1.000", "0.400,0.270,1.000", "0.431,0.249,1.000", "0.460,0.224,1.000", "0.489,0.194,1.000", "0.517,0.155,1.000", "0.545,0.097,1.000", "0.576,0.000,1.000", "0.614,0.000,1.000", "0.653,0.000,1.000", "0.693,0.000,1.000", "0.735,0.000,1.000", "0.779,0.000,1.000", "0.825,0.000,1.000", "0.873,0.000,1.000", "0.923,0.000,1.000", "0.975,0.000,1.000", "1.000,0.000,0.970", "1.000,0.000,0.918", "1.000,0.000,0.868", "1.000,0.000,0.821", "1.000,0.000,0.776", "1.000,0.000,0.732", "1.000,0.000,0.690", "1.000,0.000,0.649", "1.000,0.000,0.610", "1.000,0.000,0.571"]

# --- the bang --------------------------------------------------------

@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run particle minecraft:flash {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0 0 0 0 1 force
@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run particle minecraft:explosion_emitter {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0 0 0 0 1 force
@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run particle minecraft:end_rod {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0.1 0.1 0.1 0.35 60 force
@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run playsound minecraft:entity.generic.explode master {{player}} {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0.75 0.7
@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run playsound minecraft:block.beacon.power_select master {{player}} {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0.75 1.4
@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run playsound minecraft:entity.firework_rocket.blast master {{player}} {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0.75 1.2
@bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run playsound minecraft:item.trident.thunder master @s {{player}} {{standX}} {{bangY}} {{standZ}} 0.75 0.75

@delay 1

# --- the wheel -------------------------------------------------------

@define Int bands = rainbowColors.length()
@define Int fromBand = 0
@define Int toBand = 0
@define Int whirl = 0
@define Int seat = 0

@define Int perCentre = finaleArms / finaleCentres
@define Double armSpacing = 360D / Double(finaleArms)
@define Double centreSpacing = 360D / Double(finaleCentres)
@define Double seatSpacing = 360D / Double(perCentre)
# Each centre sits in the MIDDLE of the run of streams that feeds it, so
# they fold in from both sides instead of all sweeping one way.
@define Double centreBias = armSpacing * Double(perCentre - 1) / 2D

@define Double spinPhase = 0D
@define Double subPhase = 0D
@define Double progress = 0D
@define Double remaining = 0D
@define Double dying = 0D
@define Double gather = 0D
@define Double radius = 0D
@define Double subRadius = 0D
@define Double dustScale = finaleScale
@define Double streamAngle = 0D
@define Double centreAngle = 0D
@define Double ringAngle = 0D
@define Double subAngle = 0D
@define Double offsetX = 0D
@define Double offsetZ = 0D

@for Int i in list::range(0, finaleTicks)
    @var spinPhase = spinPhase + finaleSpin

    @if i < finaleSplitTick
        # PHASE ONE — one wave, sweeping out to the split radius. Ease
        # out: fast off the blast, slowing as it widens, arriving exactly
        # on finaleSplitTick.
        @var progress = Double(i) / Double(finaleSplitTick - 1)
        @var remaining = 1D - progress
        @var radius = finaleRadiusStart + (finaleSplitRadius - finaleRadiusStart) * (1D - remaining * remaining * remaining)
        @var dying = 0D
        @var gather = 0D
        @var subRadius = 0D
        @var dustScale = finaleScale
    @else
        # PHASE TWO — the ring hands off to finaleCentres whirls sitting
        # on it. Two things happen at once: the streams slide along the
        # ring into the centre that feeds them (gather), and they start
        # orbiting it (subRadius). Both start at zero on the split tick,
        # so the handoff is seamless — every stream is still exactly
        # where phase one left it.
        @var radius = finaleSplitRadius
        @var dying = Double(i - finaleSplitTick) / Double(finaleTicks - 1 - finaleSplitTick)
        @var subPhase = subPhase + finaleSubSpin

        @var gather = dying / finaleGather
        @if gather > 1D
            @var gather = 1D
        @fi
        @var gather = gather * gather * gather * (gather * (gather * 6D - 15D) + 10D)

        # sin(180 * dying) is 0 at the split and 0 again at the end, so
        # the orbits open out of nothing and wind back into their centre
        # rather than being cut off mid-turn.
        @var subRadius = finaleSubRadius * math::sin(180D * dying)
        @var dustScale = finaleScale * (1D - dying * dying)
    @fi

    @for Int a in list::range(0, finaleArms)
        # Which whirl this stream feeds, and its seat in that whirl's
        # orbit. Consecutive streams share a centre, so a run of the ring
        # folds into one point rather than every third stream doing so.
        @var whirl = a / perCentre
        @var seat = a % perCentre

        @var streamAngle = spinPhase + Double(a) * armSpacing
        @var centreAngle = spinPhase + Double(whirl) * centreSpacing + centreBias
        @var ringAngle = streamAngle + (centreAngle - streamAngle) * gather

        @var subAngle = subPhase + Double(seat) * seatSpacing

        @var offsetX = radius * math::cos(ringAngle) + subRadius * math::cos(subAngle)
        @var offsetZ = radius * math::sin(ringAngle) + subRadius * math::sin(subAngle)

        @var fromBand = (i * rainbowStep + a * rainbowArmOffset) % bands
        @var toBand = (fromBand + rainbowLead) % bands

        @bypass /execute in {{animWorld}} run particle dust_color_transition{from_color:[{{rainbowColors[fromBand]}}],to_color:[{{rainbowColors[toBand]}}],scale:{{dustScale}}} {{standX + offsetX}} {{finaleY}} {{standZ + offsetZ}} 0 0 0 0 1 force
    @done

    @delay 1
@done
